      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T08:07:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this necessary? I think what you\u0027re trying to do here is ensure that when we run the tethering MTS suite, that we also run the integration tests in addition to the CTS tests. But you don\u0027t need to do this by including the tests in this build target. You can also do it by changing the MTS tethering test plan to run both MtsTetheringTest and the tethering CTS tests. I think al you need is to add:\n\n    test_suites: [\n        \"mts-tethering\",\n    ],\n\nto the CtsTetheringTest build rule.\n\nEven better - if the intent is to run all the tethering CTS tests in MTS in addition to the tests in Tethering/tests/mts/... then why keep a separate MtsTetheringTest target and directory at all? There\u0027s only one file in Tethering/tests/mts/... , and we could just move it under Tethering/tests/cts/. Then we could delete MtsTetheringTest and Tethering/tests/mts/ entirely.\n\nThat doesn\u0027t need to be in this CL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "75f02a454b066a9e6b22bf44dfc76de14dc2a045",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa31d973_32bc7407",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/mts/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T02:52:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the MTS should cover CTS which means MTS is CTS + some tests to test mainline module behavior but not related to API (e.g. test whether private address selection is expected). For most of OEM, move Tethering/tests/mts/ to Tethering/tests/cts/ is fine because tethering is mandatory mainline module. But this is not correct for china devices which do not adopt tethering mainline module. This is why I still want to maintain two tests target CtsTetheringTest and MtsTetheringTest. And make MtsTetheringTest include all of CtsTEtheringTest.",
      "parentUuid": "34627a2d_45df6734",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "75f02a454b066a9e6b22bf44dfc76de14dc2a045",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3023ac28_60e45dd9",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/mts/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T11:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why can\u0027t we just have all the tests in one suite though? Is there a reason the tests right now in mts/ *shouldn\u0027t* be in cts/? We already have lots of test targets and it would be good to reduce the number if we can. And I don\u0027t think we have a separate MTS directory for any of the other modules.\n\nFor this CL, is it feasible to use the suggestion above and add \"mts-tethering\" to the test suites of the other target instead of including the code from the other target into this target? That should at least reduce the amount of code that needs to be built to run the tests.",
      "parentUuid": "fa31d973_32bc7407",
